The kernel implementations follow well-documented prior art:

- The fused-softmax kernel structurally matches Triton's own
  `02-fused-softmax.py` tutorial. The implementation here was
  written from specification (not copy-pasted), and the structure
  is the canonical one any Triton tutorial would teach.

- The fused-rmsnorm kernel is the standard single-pass formulation
  with no novel claim attached.

- The flash-attention v2 forward kernel implements the
  online-softmax algorithm from Dao 2023 (arXiv:2307.08691). The
  implementation here is fp32 forward-only; the full FA-v2 paper
  covers backward, fp16, and tensor-core paths that this v0.1.0
  does not.

This repo claims no novel kernel work. The artifact is the
benchmark harness + honest correctness + performance reporting on
a small consumer Turing GPU, not the kernels themselves.

